## Explicit Deep Copying

```xiom
pub interface Clone {
  fn clone(self: &Self) -> Self;
}
```

Clone is for values that can be explicitly duplicated:

```xiom
pub type Document = {
  title: Str;
  body: Str;
}

impl Clone for Document {
  fn clone(self: &Document) -> Document {
    return Document{
      title: self.title.clone(),
      body: self.body.clone(),
    };
  }
}

fn main() {
  let original = Document{ title: "Draft", body: "Hello" };
  let copy = original.clone();  // Deep copy
  // original and copy are independent
}
```

### Clone vs Move

```xiom
let a = Vec[Int](); a.push(1); a.push(2);
let b = a;          // MOVE: a is gone, b owns the data
let c = a.clone();  // CLONE: a stays, c gets its own copy
```

### Auto-Deriving Clone

```xiom
// All fields must implement Clone
#[derive(Clone)]
pub type Point = { x: Float64; y: Float64; }
```

### When NOT to Clone
Cloning a large Vec duplicates all memory — use references (`&T`) or `Arc[T]` for shared data instead.

